# The COMPLETE never-commit set, and ONLY that set, so the orchestrator can
# `git add -A` safely every checkpoint and end with a clean tree. Everything else
# the factory produces (the progress ledger, gate evidence, reports, the static
# architecture-map data, source-map, coverage report, catalog/traceability JSON)
# IS committed. The architecture map is a STATIC graph generated once at
# extraction; live per-issue progress lives in the ledger and is projected onto the
# static graph at read time, so the map file stays unchanged across the dev-loop.
node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store

# SECRETS ARE NEVER COMMITTED — `git add -A` at every checkpoint would commit and push real values. The whole family is ignored and re-included NOWHERE: the managed block is appended at EOF, so the first marker repair would land it below any `!` line and flip that line for good. The placeholder template `.env.example` is in history because scaffold TRACKS it (git add -f), which no ignore rule can undo.
.env
.env.*

# Vivicy factory runtime + per-issue parallel worktrees.
.vivicy-runtime/
.vivicy-worktrees/

# The parallel loop's transient integration mutex — created/removed during a merge,
# never part of history (committing its churn would dirty the tree).
.vivicy/development/gates/.integration.lock

# TRANSCRIPTS ARE NEVER COMMITTED (full agent session JSONL; the ledger links to
# them, they never enter git history).
.vivicy/development/transcripts/

# PROOF ARTIFACTS ARE NEVER COMMITTED (per-issue observations of the real run —
# captures, request transcripts, run logs). Each proof's recipe.txt IS committed:
# an observation is replayable by anyone only if its command lives in history, and
# a directory pattern cannot be re-included from, hence the three-line form.
.vivicy/development/proofs/**
!.vivicy/development/proofs/**/
!.vivicy/development/proofs/**/recipe.txt
